    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm 35 and i've never really lifted weights before so i'm looking to start a simple routine. can you put together a 4 week linear progression program for me? i want to focus on the main compound lifts like squats, bench, and deadlifts to get a good base. just a basic schedule of what to do and how to progress each week.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Starting with compound lifts is a fantastic way to build a strong foundation! For your first four weeks, focus on mastering form with moderate weight. Aim for 3 sets of 5 repetitions for squats, bench press, and deadlifts each workout. Progress by adding a small amount of weight (e.g., 2.5-5 lbs) to the bar each week provided you maintain excellent form throughout your sets.",
