    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds doable. what about when i'm actually in the middle of a set and everything feels impossible? like my muscles are burning and my brain is telling me to just quit. how do i handle that mental wall so i don't give up on the program?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When you hit that mental wall, focus on controlled breathing to calm your nervous system. Remind yourself of your goal, and instead of aiming to finish the rep perfectly, focus only on completing the next single repetition. Often, just giving yourself permission to push through *one more* repetition is enough to break through the sticking point.",
      "source": "target",
